## JavaScript modules

A **module** is bundled JavaScript that your script can import. The Markdown attribute `uses` takes exact module keys separated by spaces. For example, `uses="diagram@1"` makes `await import("diagram")` available. A type already includes the modules in its table row. The editor’s Modules picker offers additional libraries. You can leave `uses` out when the type supplies everything your script needs. Each saved document version retains the module code it used.

| Module key for `uses` | Name for `await import()` |
|---|---|
<% catalog.libraries.each_key do |key| -%>
| `<%= key %>` | `"<%= key.split("@").first %>"` |
<% end -%>

